      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Since 3 and -2 are roots, we know that\n\n$$(x-3)(x+2) = x^2 - x - 6.$$\n\nThen by long division or synthetic division, we find the third root using\n\n$$ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = a(x^2 - x - 6)(x-r)$$for some $r \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $a\\neq 0.$ Multiplying out the right side, we get\n\n\\begin{align*}\nax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d &= a(x^3-x^2-6x-rx^2+rx+6r) \\\\\n&=a(x^3+(1-6-r)x^2+(1-6)rx+6r) \\\\\n&=a(x^3+(1+r-6)x^2-(4+6+r)rx+6r).\n\\end{align*}\n\nFrom this, we want to compare coefficients of corresponding powers of $x.$ Since $a\\neq 0,$ we have\n\n$$b=a(1+r-6), \\quad c=a(4+6+r), \\quad\\text{and}\\quad d=a6r.$$\n\nThus,\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{c}{b} &= \\frac{a(4+6+r)}{a(1+r-6)} = \\frac{10+r}{1+r-6} = \\frac{1+r}{-5-r} = \\frac{1+r}{-(5+r)}, \\\\\n\\frac{b}{a} &= \\frac{1+r-6}{1+r-6} = \\frac{-5}{-5} = 1.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinally, we compute\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{b}{a}+\\frac{c}{a} &= \\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{1 + \\frac{1+r}{-5-r}}{1} = \\frac{1-1/5}{1} = \\boxed{\\frac{4}{5}}.\n\\end{align*}",
